><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250502170032+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250502170036+10'00'" name="33bc8da2-7957-4186-b55f-8056573bc6cc" page="15" coords="303.667053,718.473877,550.400757,718.473877,303.667053,706.342590,550.400757,706.342590,303.667053,707.016907,550.400879,707.016907,303.667053,694.885620,550.400879,694.885620,303.667053,695.559937,550.400940,695.559937,303.667053,683.428650,550.400940,683.428650,303.667053,684.101929,550.401428,684.101929,303.667053,671.970642,550.401428,671.970642,303.667053,672.644958,550.400635,672.644958,303.667053,660.513672,550.400635,660.513672,303.667053,661.187988,550.401550,661.187988,303.667053,649.056702,550.401550,649.056702,303.667053,649.731018,550.400574,649.731018,303.667053,637.599731,550.400574,637.599731,303.667053,638.274048,550.400757,638.274048,303.667053,626.142761,550.400757,626.142761,303.667053,626.817078,550.400879,626.817078,303.667053,614.685791,550.400879,614.685791,303.667053,615.360107,550.401489,615.360107,303.667053,603.228821,550.401489,603.228821,303.667053,603.903137,366.680939,603.903137,303.667053,591.771851,366.680939,591.771851,44.980042,112.150833,291.713745,112.150833,44.980042,100.019547,291.713745,100.019547,44.980042,100.693832,291.714539,100.693832,44.980042,88.562546,291.714539,88.562546" rect="44.600937,88.183441,550.780640,718.852966" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Mean power was found to be lower in comparison to the&#xD;Reference System for all devices. Magnitudes of negative&#xD;systematic error were similar for Peach, Weba, and the Concept2,&#xD;but larger for EmPower. Stroke-to-stroke variations in power&#xD;were consistent between Peach and the Reference System, but&#xD;a small reduction in measurement sensitivity was evident for&#xD;the Concept2, whereas EmPower and Weba introduced noise.&#xD;There was some evidence of between-unit differences in mean&#xD;power for Peach, EmPower, and Weba, and in the SD of power&#xD;(stroke-to-stroke fluctuations) for Weba. The findings of this&#xD;study can be used by practitioners to inform the interpretation&#xD;of meaningful change in measures of power when using the&#xD;devices assessed.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="15" rect="488.947601,380.908081,673.530273,718.655029"
/></highlight
